-@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
-+# Floorplan in other coding agents
-+
-+Floorplan is one skill (`skills/floorplan/`) plus plain Node scripts, so any agent that loads Agent Skills can run it.
-+Claude Code and Codex install it as a plugin (see [Getting started](getting-started.md) and [Codex](codex.md)).
-+For the others, clone this repository once and link the skill folder where that agent looks for skills.
-+Nothing here downloads or runs anything on its own; a link is the whole install.
-+
-+```bash
-+git clone https://github.com/<you>/floorplan ~/floorplan
-+```
-+
-+| Agent | Where skills live | Command |
-+|---|---|---|
-+| Cursor | discovered from `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json` when the repo is opened, or Settings → Plugins | open the clone in Cursor once, or add it from the Plugins search |
-+| VS Code + GitHub Copilot (1.108+) | `.copilot-plugin/plugin.json`, or `~/.copilot/skills` | `ln -s ~/floorplan/skills/floorplan ~/.copilot/skills/floorplan` |
-+| Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Pi | `~/.agents/skills` | `ln -s ~/floorplan/skills/floorplan ~/.agents/skills/floorplan` |
-+| Cline | `~/.cline/skills` | `ln -s ~/floorplan/skills/floorplan ~/.cline/skills/floorplan` |
-+| Kiro | `~/.kiro/skills` | `ln -s ~/floorplan/skills/floorplan ~/.kiro/skills/floorplan` |
-+| Trae | `~/.trae/skills` | `ln -s ~/floorplan/skills/floorplan ~/.trae/skills/floorplan` |
-+| Anything else with a shell | — | ask it to read `~/floorplan/skills/floorplan/SKILL.md` and follow it |
-+
-+On Windows use `mklink /J <target> %USERPROFILE%\floorplan\skills\floorplan` in place of `ln -s`.
-+Update with `git -C ~/floorplan pull`; the link keeps pointing at the new version.
-+
-+What works everywhere: the map, Health, screens, flows, `trace`, `impact`, and `node floorplan/query.mjs context | fn | map | erd`,
-+which is how any agent saves tokens on later tasks. The map's **Ask** bar answers through the Claude Code CLI or Codex
-+when one of them is installed; without either, the map still works and Ask explains what it needs.
-+In agents where `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}` isn't filled in, it means the folder holding SKILL.md (the skill says so).
