-+If the user writes to you in a language other than English, or asks for one, set `"language": "<that language>"` (e.g. `"Japanese"`, `"Urdu"`) in architecture.json. Names, descriptions, summaries, flows, the tour and recent-work notes are then written in it (describe.mjs worksheets say so), and Ask answers in it. Paths and code names stay as they are. For the map's own buttons and labels, the build writes the English list to `floorplan/.cache/ui-strings.en.json` and reports `UI STRINGS`: translate it once into `floorplan/ui-strings.json` as `{ "English": "translation" }` (keep it short and natural, leave product names like Floorplan, Claude and Codex as they are) and build again. It's kept on every update.
